{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":638,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:2Chr.12","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"2 Chronicles","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"2 Chronicles 12","reference":"2 Chronicles 12","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Rehoboam forsaking God is oppressed by Shishak, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-4.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"He humbles himself, and is preserved in his kingdom, but spoiled of his treasures, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"6-12.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"His character and death, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"13-16.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"And all Israel - So called, because they forsook God, as Israel had done.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":10,"text":"Fifth year - Presently after the apostacy of the king and people, which was in the fourth year.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":11,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"Lubims - A people of Africk bordering upon Egypt.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":13,"text":"Sukkiims - A people living in tents, as the word signifies; and such there were not far from Egypt, both in Africk and in Arabia.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":14,"text":"Ethiopians - Either those beyond Egypt, or the Arabians.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":15,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":16,"text":"Some deliverance - I will give some stop to the course of my wrath, which was ready to be poured forth upon them to their utter destruction.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":17,"text":"Those who acknowledge God is righteous in afflicting them, shall find him gracious.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":18,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":19,"text":"May know - That they may experimentally know the difference between my yoke and the yoke of a foreign and idolatrous prince.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":20,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":21,"text":"Went well - The began to recruity themselves, and regain some degree of their former prosperity.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":22,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":23,"text":"Did evil - Or, settled not, although he humbled himself, for a season, yet he quickly relapsed into sin, because his heart was not right with God.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":12}}